//? Title: Periodic Lax–Wendroff advection
//? Subtitle: Actual stencils, the original Gaussian and explicit stability controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A second-order centered transport update conserves periodic mass in exact
arithmetic and is L2 stable under its Courant restriction. Those facts do not
imply positivity or absence of ringing. We inspect the actual producing
stencils, retain the original200-cell Gaussian experiment and compare actual
Fourier-mode growth and smooth-grid refinement with their mathematical
references.
)

\toc

> From transport to the stencil

For u_t+a*u_x=0, Taylor expansion in time and u_tt=a^2*u_xx give

$$u_j^{k+1}=u_j^k-\frac{\nu}{2}(u_{j+1}^k-u_{j-1}^k)+\frac{\nu^2}{2}(u_{j+1}^k-2u_j^k+u_{j-1}^k),\quad\nu=a\Delta t/\Delta x.$$
\alttext(Every new cell uses three values from the complete previous periodic state, with Courant coefficient nu.)

Indices wrap periodically. The first difference approximates transport, and the
second comes from the time expansion rather than an arbitrary smoothing knob.
Summing the periodic differences gives zero, hence exact-arithmetic mass
conservation. The implementation uses separate old/new buffers; all displayed
operands and results come from this producing execution.

> One actual impulse update

Set nu=0.5 and initial values0,0,1,0,0. The new values include −0.125,
immediately disproving positivity preservation despite the stable Courant value.
Native records expose the exact contributing old values and both terms.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lax_impulse.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lax_wendroff.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lax_wendroff_trace({0, 0, 1, 0, 0}, 1, 1, .5, 1);
    std::print("| actual cell | actual left | actual center | actual right | subtractive term | additive " "term | actual new value |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &c : t.cells)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", c.index, c.left,
                   c.center, c.right, c.advective_term, c.diffusive_term,
                   c.value);
    std::print("\nActual mass {} to {}; actual L2 {} to {}.\n",
               t.diagnostics.front().mass, t.diagnostics.back().mass,
               t.diagnostics.front().l2_norm, t.diagnostics.back().l2_norm);
    auto c = t.cells[1];
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("old", {0, 2},
           std::format("Actual old stencil\n{}, {}, {}", c.left, c.center,
                       c.right)).node("terms", {0, -2},
                                      std::format("Actual subtract/add terms\n{}, {}",
                                                  c.advective_term,
                                                  c.diffusive_term)).node(
        "new", {7, 0}, std::format("Actual cell{} output\n{}", c.index, c.value)).edge("old", "new").edge("terms", "new").save_svg("build/lax_impulse.svg");
}
```
