> L2 stability and an explicit unstable control

For a Fourier mode exp(i*j*theta), the exact-arithmetic amplification factor is

$$G=1-i\nu\sin\theta+\nu^2(\cos\theta-1),\qquad |G|^2=1-4\nu^2(1-\nu^2)\sin^4(\theta/2).$$
\alttext(The squared amplification is at most one for every Fourier angle when the absolute Courant coefficient is at most one.)

Thus abs(nu)<=1 gives L2 stability, not an L-infinity maximum principle,
positivity or monotonicity. At computed nu0 and plus/minus1, native exact copy
paths avoid cancellation: identity or one-cell periodic shift. Default calls
reject a Courant violation. The following explicit allow_unstable control
intentionally permits nu1.2 to show growth of a32-cell alternating Nyquist mode;
the stable nu0.8 control decays. The symbol is a theoretical reference, while
every plotted norm comes from the actual stored states.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lax_fourier.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lax_wendroff.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <cmath>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> u(32);
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < u.size(); ++j)
        u[j] = j % 2 ? -1 : 1;
    bool rejected = false;
    try {
        dm::algorithms::lax_wendroff_advection(u, 1, 1, 1.2, 1);
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        rejected = true;
    }
    std::print("Default Courant1.2 rejected: {}.\n\n| actual Courant | actual step | actual L2 ratio | " "analytic absolute G power |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n",
               rejected);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    for (double nu : {.8, 1.2}) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::lax_wendroff_trace(u, 1, 1, nu, 12, true);
        double g =
            std::abs(dm::algorithms::lax_wendroff_amplification(nu,
                                                                std::numbers::pi));
        std::vector<double> x, y, reference;
        for (std::size_t k = 0; k < t.states.size(); ++k) {
            double ratio = t.diagnostics[k].l2_norm / t.diagnostics[0].l2_norm;
            std::print("| {} | {} | {:.12g} | {:.12g} |\n", nu, k, ratio,
                       std::pow(g, k));
            x.push_back(k);
            y.push_back(std::log10(ratio));
            reference.push_back(std::log10(std::pow(g, k)));
        }
        auto color =
            nu < 1 ? dm::graphics::RGB{37, 99, 235}
            : dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38};
        p.line(x, reference, std::format("symbol nu{}", nu), color, 1.5).points(
            x, y, std::format("actual nu{}", nu), color, 4);
    }
    p.y_limits(-8, 7).title("Actual stable decay and explicit unstable growth").x_label("actual completed steps").y_label("log10(actual L2 divided by initial L2)").save_svg("build/lax_fourier.svg");
}
```
