\caption(Actual complete smooth-grid runs with observed convergence orders.)
\alttext(The measured errors are distinct from the explicitly anchored theoretical slope; update counts report the real quadratic work along this fixed-Courant refinement.)

> Contracts and verification

Inputs must be finite and nonempty, speed finite, spacing positive finite,
timestep nonnegative finite, and steps nonnegative. Full input, work geometry
and CFL policy are checked before computation. Ordinary finite double operation
order is retained; nonfinite intermediate arithmetic triggers a widened fallback
whose finite double output is still checked. Explicit unstable mode can still
throw on produced overflow. Count-only analysis avoids additional state
diagnostics. Trace diagnostics use widened time, mass and L2 arithmetic and add
measured observation work.

Complete capture admission counts n+1+steps*(2*n+1) logical entries before
copies or updates: original values and diagnostic, then each new state,
diagnostic and producing cell records. The million-entry default excludes record
fields, capacities, final-result/runtime copies and bytes/RAM; zero disables
only that optional cap. Captures own their inputs and every actual state. No
prefix reruns reconstruct history.

Independent exact Fraction arithmetic verified100 advection studies and741
actual states, including their mass and L2 observations. Another1000 ordinary
nonunit-Courant trajectories matched the frozen outputs bitwise. Native tests
verify actual impulse stencils, exact copy paths, overflow fallback, full
guards/quotas, Fourier amplification and explicit unstable growth, the original
Gaussian and smooth sine refinement. The complete ten-report batch passed77
native CTest cases,39 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases,106
compiled/executed public examples,479/479 scoped definitions and ten
representative clangd hovers. All4 complete report programs executed and all4
native figures were visually reviewed. HTML/Markdown computed result and
identical source/build/export figure bytes passed verification. Repeatable
receipts are retained under `build/mepml-conversion/batch-194-203/`.

> References

P. Lax and B. Wendroff(1960),
[Systems of Conservation Laws|https://doi.org/10.1002/cpa.3160130205],
Communications on Pure and Applied Mathematics13(2),217–237. The scalar periodic
constant-speed scheme is the specific case examined here; no shock monotonicity
or nonlinear convergence claim follows from the Fourier calculation.
